Written by hand for this repository on 2026-11-19 (CC0 1.0: no rights
reserved), no third-party content. A KiCad 10 design holding one of every
schematic item kind that is not a symbol, for sch.item.get, sch.item.set,
sch.image.place and ev.schItem (unit m5-i, tests/e2e/sch-items.spec.ts).
The three schematic files were written in KiCad 10's text form and then
saved once by KiCad's own schematic writer (kicad-cli 10.0 "sch upgrade",
kicad/kicad:10.0, 2026-11-19), so each is KiCad's normalized form; the
project file is hand written. The picture is an 8 by 8 PNG made for this
fixture.

- items-sch.kicad_sch, the root (uuid ...0100): three wires meeting at a
  junction (...0110, ...0111, ...0112, junction ...0118) with a no connect
  (...0119) at the free end of the first; a bus (...0115) with a bus entry
  (...0116), the wire (...0113) and the label D0 (...011c) beside it and the
  bus label D[0..3] (...011b); the local label IN1 (...011a) on the third
  wire's end; the global label GOUT (...011e, shape input, its
  Intersheetrefs field); the hierarchical label HIER (...011f, output); a
  directive label (...0120, round, its Netclass field Default); a text
  "Items" (...0121); a text box (...0122); a graphic line (...0123, dashed);
  a rectangle (...0140); a rule area of four corners (...0141); the picture
  (...0144); a 2 by 2 table (...012f, cells ...0130 to ...0133 reading A, B,
  C and empty); the group "Pair" (...0160) of the text and the rectangle;
  and the sheet "sub" (...0150, file sub.kicad_sch, page 2) with one sheet
  pin A_PIN (...0151, input, left).
- sub.kicad_sch (uuid ...0200): the hierarchical label A_PIN (...0201).
- spare.kicad_sch (uuid ...0300): a file of the project no sheet shows (one
  text, ...0301), so a sheet's file set to it exists.
- items-sch.kicad_pro names the root and the sheet sub.

Every uuid above is cc05a11e-0000-4000-8000- followed by the twelve digits
shown. Read by kicad-cli 10.0 (2026-11-19): both sheets of the hierarchy
load; ERC reports only the connection findings of a drawing with no parts
(dangling labels, pins left unconnected, two names on one net). files.json lists what the e2e harness
opens. The KiCad files carry no comment (their formats have none), so this
file holds their license.
